# The pod door's READ-ONLY rows, one `name=port` per line (backlog
# 9a440539, 2026-10-01): every boss-ports service the LAN machine door
# (infra/forge/sor-ports.env) does not carry and the boss pod serves off
# loopback. infra/dev/boss-api reaches each on the host in ./sor-read-url
# — the in-cluster boss-read-internal Service — and sends it GET only:
# any other method to one of these rows is refused before curl, because
# what this table exists for is measuring live data, and widening what
# a WRITE may reach is a decision of its own (each LAN row carries its
# reason in boss-jobs-internal.yaml).
#
# A copy, pinned (CLAUDE.md §9a):
# crates/core/boss-testing/tests/every_boss_ports_service_has_a_door.rs
# holds these lines equal to boss-ports and to the manifest
# (infra/cluster/manifests/boss-read-internal.yaml), ./sor-read-url to
# that manifest's name, and holds this table, the LAN table and the
# named loopback-only set to a partition of boss-ports — so a new
# service is refused until it is placed on a door or named off one.
#
# Read as data (`#` and blank lines dropped), never sourced.
shipping=7100
messages=7200
inventory=7300
commerce=7400
assets=7600
catalog=7750
clock=7060
products=7840
campaigns=7845
customers=7855
